<title>GERMANY: RTRS-Opel appoints GM-H man chief financial officer.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Opel appoints GM-H man chief financial officer.</headline>
<dateline>RUESSELSHEIM, Germany 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Adam Opel AG, the German unit of U.S. carmaker General Motors Corp, said on Friday that Hennig Klages will become its new chief financial officer on September 1.</p>
<p>Klages, 57, has been director of finance and strategic planning at GM's Holden Automotive in Australia since 1994.</p>
<p>Klages joined GM in 1956 at its South African subsidiary and has worked for the carmaker in London, Detroit and in Germany.</p>
<p>He was treasurer of Opel from 1984 to 1987.</p>
</text>
